# Astrolabe ESP MCP

When debugging Astrolabe on hardware:

## Device console

| Need | MCP tool |
|------|----------|
| Boot log, `Serial`, ESP_LOG, panics | **`astrolabe_serial_monitor`** (USB CDC 115200) |
| Serial + confirm JTAG adapter | **`astrolabe_console_monitor`** |
| OpenOCD link only | **`astrolabe_jtag_openocd`** |
| Halt, backtrace, inject face | **`astrolabe_jtag_gdb`** / **`astrolabe_debug_gdb`** |

JTAG does **not** stream printf — always pair GDB with **`astrolabe_serial_monitor`** (or `./scripts/monitor_serial.sh` in a second terminal).

1. **`astrolabe_list_ports`** — confirm `/dev/cu.usbmodem*` before upload/monitor.
2. **`astrolabe_serial_monitor`** — `reset_boot: true` for fresh boot log; logs under `artifacts/monitor/`.
3. **`astrolabe_upload`** / **`astrolabe_build`** — flash `waveshare_s3_175` (or `_debug` for GDB).

## Clock-face QA

Follow [hardware-qa.mdc](hardware-qa.mdc): upload → show face → `screen.bmp` → evaluate.

Reload MCP if tools are missing (`mcp/astrolabe-esp/setup.sh`, entry in `~/.cursor/mcp.json`).
